  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1206 PM MDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nUpper high stretching from southern NV to our area throughout the \nday. Elevated wildfire smoke from Washington and Oregon has been \nreaching our area the last couple days bringing hazy skies. This \nmornings cloud cover and showers have been slowly eroding away. \nDepending on how fast the cloud cover clears out, this may hinder \nsome thunderstorm activity. Hi-res CAMs models are still suggesting \nan uptick in storm activity this afternoon starting in the area \nmountains around noon with outflows triggering off more storms in \nthe lowlands later this afternoon. Gusty outflow winds, blowing \ndust, and some flooding possible. Upper high shifts ever so slightly \nto the Four Corners Friday. Residual moisture trapped under the high \nwill bring another round of afternoon monsoonal thunderstorms \nFriday. \n\nUpper high stays put over the Four Corners through the weekend with \ndrier air from the Great Plains pushing in, limiting storm chances \nto just the area mountains. Heading into early next week, the upper \nhigh looks to shift southward centering over AZ/NM but moisture \ntrapped under this high should continue to bring daily afternoon \nstorm chances.",
